# The stamping line with one motor instead of two, which is not half a stamping
# line.
#
# One motor makes 54 rotary and the shaft splits it fairly: 27 to the rolling
# mill, 27 to the crank. The mill is happy to run slowly and does. The crank is
# happy to run slowly and does, at 23 strokes a tick. The press is not -- a
# press fed half the strokes it needs does not make half a gear, it fails to
# close -- and a stroke that arrives unused does not queue for later. It has
# happened.
#
# So the press waits for the crank's own ram to gather past thirty, fires, and
# waits again: 18 gears a tick against 08-stamping's 49, on half the motors,
# with 15 heat a tick of strokes falling on nothing. Half the drive bought a
# third of the gears and missed the brief.

machine "One Motor"
brief gears

inlet     I1  at 0,0   draws iron
inlet     I2  at 0,4   draws coal
furnace   F1  at 4,0
burner    B1  at 4,5
rollmill  R1  at 10,0
press     P1  at 15,0
outlet    O1  at 20,0

crank     CR1 at 15,5
shaft     SH1 at 10,4
motor     MO1 at 10,7
mains     M1  at 10,10

wire I1.out -> F1.in
wire I2.out -> B1.fuel
wire B1.heat -> F1.heat
wire F1.out -> R1.in
wire R1.out -> P1.in
wire P1.out -> O1.solid

wire M1.power -> MO1.power
wire MO1.rotary -> SH1.in
wire SH1.out -> R1.drive
wire SH1.out -> CR1.drive
wire CR1.stroke -> P1.drive
